  nonce: 482f  # 482f
  message: "PR #248 MERGED (dev e3f59ed2e2). ITEM STAYS VIOLATED — read why before closing.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED: derived confidence now re-derives from finalize's resolution\nverdict instead of the producer's advisory flag.\n`finalize._rederive_confidence_from_verdict`, called from\n`_finalize_edge_resolution` for every edge.\n\nCLOSURE EVIDENCE (re-run on the merged tree, caddy):\n  stale-at-resolved-base   6,167 -> 0\n  unresolved-after-finalize 13,637 -> 13,637   (unchanged: nothing was\n                                                reclassified, only corrected)\nPre-merge, all four repos: caddy 6,167, mitmproxy 8,880, poetry 4,074,\nalertmanager 3,922 = 23,043 edges, two languages, two evidence types\n(ast_call 0.85->0.40, ast_call_direct 0.85->0.50).\n\nDIRECTION, measured on caddy: 6,140 DOWN, 0 UP, 0 resolved edges changed.\nreceiver_blind_magnets bands at 0.80 and was the obvious exposure, but its\ncontract requires is_resolved=True, so this change cannot add or remove a magnet\nfinding — structurally, not just observationally. Its 0-in-both-arms reading was\nan UNEXERCISED INSTRUMENT and is recorded as such, not as evidence of safety.\nslice's min_confidence defaults to 0.0, so no default view loses an edge.\n\n*** WHY THIS DOES NOT CLOSE THE ITEM ***\n\nThis item's STATEMENT describes a live taint FP channel: an edge carrying\nis_resolved=True at an external dst reaching the ungated hits[0] bare-name\nfallback. That channel is closed by different means (finalize sub-step 7), and\nPR #248 did not touch it. What #248 fixed is the defect found UNDERNEATH it\nduring re-measurement. Marking this satisfied would credit the fix to the wrong\nmechanism.\n\nBOTH OBVIOUS MEASUREMENTS OF THE FILED CHANNEL ARE TAUTOLOGIES, and both were\nreached in this project before the real number was:\n  - AFTER finalize: 0 of 125,007 edges across 9 repos — finalize DEFINES THE\n    PREDICATE AWAY, so the probe measures finalize's own overwrite.\n  - BEFORE finalize: also 0 — the flag has not flipped yet.\nThe defect is visible only by running the resolution sub-step and THEN comparing\nconfidence against the verdict. Do not close on either zero; that is the\nINV-nufob false-close shape, and a proposed `satisfiable_now` verdict for this\nitem was inverted 2/2 by adversarial re-measurement.\n\nTO ACTUALLY CLOSE: either (a) demonstrate the filed channel is unreachable with\na NON-tautological instrument (one that does not measure post-finalize state),\nor (b) refile the statement onto the mechanism that was real. (b) is the honest\noption and is what the mechanism note above sets up.\n\nSTILL OPEN, unresolved: whether this shares a root cause with WI-kamin (Go\ninitializer typing hijacking 118/692 moved edges onto the wrong in-repo symbol).\nNot determined."  # 482f
- op: discuss  # 0397
  at: '2026-08-10T02:43:23Z'  # 0397
  by: agent  # 0397
