  clock: 6  # 0397
  nonce: '0397'  # 0397
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-08-09, NOT STALE -- the filed repro reproduces byte-for-byte and\nthe downstream escape it depends on is still live. Recorded as positive evidence\nbecause a note elsewhere in my working context claimed this item's defect was\n'confidence fossilization, FIXED in #248', which would have made it look closable.\nIt is not.\n\nFILED REPRO, re-run on merged dev:\n\n  two-step  tr := &http.Transport{}; tr.RoundTrip(req)\n            dst=go:external:0-0:RoundTrip:unresolved\n            is_resolved=TRUE   confidence=0.85  meta={'call_construct':'method','receiver':'external'}\n\n  chained   (&http.Transport{}).RoundTrip(req)\n            dst=go:external:0-0:RoundTrip:unresolved      <- BYTE-IDENTICAL dst\n            is_resolved=FALSE  confidence=0.4   meta={'call_construct':'method'}\n\nExactly as this item states: an edge carrying no module evidence (path segment\n'external', kind 'unresolved') is reported is_resolved=True, and the same call\nwritten the other way is not.\n\nTHE DOWNSTREAM HALF IS ALSO STILL LIVE, which is what makes the flag consequential\nrather than cosmetic. taint.py:461 branches on is_resolved; at :484 it computes\n_module_from_symbol_path(edge_dst), which finds no path evidence for an\n'external' path segment; at :485-489 it takes the documented legacy escape\n`if not path_module: return hits[0]` -- an UNGATED bare-name match. gate_named_entry,\nwhich would refuse an untyped method call, is never reached. WI-damir tightened the\nis_resolved branch but that no-path-evidence escape survives, and it is precisely the\none an 'external' dst lands on.\n\nWHAT #248 DID AND DID NOT DO: confidence differs across the two arms (0.85 vs 0.4),\nwhich is the fossilization angle. The is_resolved discrepancy -- the thing this\nitem's STATEMENT is about -- is untouched.\n\nStatus stays violated. The thread's existing guidance is unchanged and still right:\nboth obvious measurements of the filed channel are tautologies, so do NOT close on\neither zero; close by (a) a non-tautological instrument or (b) refiling the statement\nonto the mechanism that was real."  # 0397
- op: discuss  # cb30
  at: '2026-08-10T04:51:02Z'  # cb30
  by: agent  # cb30
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cb30
  clock: 7  # cb30
  nonce: cb30  # cb30
  message: "PRODUCER LINE LOCALIZED, AND PARTLY CLOSED, 2026-08-10 (Go composite-literal PR).\n\nThis item recorded that the producer half was never localized. It is go.py's WI-jopar\nreceiver guard (was go.py:2572-2592 on dev c675fc484f). That guard fires when the\nreceiver is a bare identifier present in var_types -- INCLUDING the empty-string entry\nthe neighbouring comment describes for \"composite_literal of qualified_type\", i.e.\nexactly the &http.Transport{} / &http.Client{} case -- and calls Edge.create with NO\nis_resolved= argument, so it takes the True default (ir.py:832, 877) onto a dst whose\nkind slot reads `unresolved`. The chained spelling (&http.Transport{}).RoundTrip(req)\nhas a non-identifier operand, misses this branch, and lands on an emit site that passes\nis_resolved=False explicitly. Identical dst, identical call_construct, opposite verdicts\n-- which is this item's filed asymmetry.\n\nCLOSED AT THAT LINE by the composite-literal PR: the guard now states is_resolved=False.\nNot a courtesy fix -- the PR makes the guard fire far more often, so leaving it would\nhave widened the channel. Producer-stage is_resolved=True falls by 10,319 across\n6 Go repos (dnscrypt-proxy, act, grype, cosign, kserve, caddy).\n\nSTILL OPEN: three sibling emission sites carry the same omission (the chained-call\nambiguity guard, the short-name ambiguity guard, the unexported-method visibility\nguard). Not touched -- out of that PR's blast radius.\n\nCONSUMER HALF, VERIFIED IN CODE RATHER THAN INHERITED: finalize.py sub-step 7\n(_finalize_edge_resolution, finalize.py:404-427) re-derives is_resolved from the dst\nnode's kind and overwrites the producer verdict -- kind != external_symbol => True, else\nFalse. So a producer-stage True is provably gone before taint runs, which reconciles the\ntwo readings already on this thread: the taint.py hits[0] escape is live CODE, but no Go\nexternal method edge reaches it in a full pipeline run. The producer defect is real and\nworth closing for coherence; the exploitability claim through taint is NOT supported."  # cb30
