- op: discuss  # 130d
  at: '2026-08-10T13:52:33Z'  # 130d
  by: agent  # 130d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 130d
  clock: 9  # 130d
  nonce: 130d  # 130d
  message: "PRODUCER HALF CLOSED AT EVERY SITE, 2026-08-10. ITEM STAYS VIOLATED — read why\nbefore closing, because this thread has already recorded two tautological\nmeasurements of this channel and this note is deliberately not a third.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. All four go.py emit sites that could mint is_resolved=True onto a\ndst carrying the `external` path placeholder now state the flag. Two sites\nalready did (the field-chain guard and the WI-jopar receiver guard, the latter\nwith a comment naming this item); the remaining four did not:\n\n  2763  ambiguity guard        (2+ in-repo candidates)   -> is_resolved=False\n  2794  visibility guard       (lowercase method)        -> is_resolved=False\n  2822  stdlib-interface guard (Close/Lock/Read/...)     -> is_resolved=False\n  3964  route-mount dispatch   -> is_resolved MIRRORS THE BRANCH (resolved when\n        the handler is an in-repo symbol, False when it falls back to the\n        placeholder). A blanket False here would have been as wrong as the\n        inherited True.\n\nLIVE REPROS, analyzer stage, BEFORE the fix — this is the non-tautological\nevidence the thread asks for, because it is taken before finalize runs at all:\n\n  items[0].Handle()   dst=go:external:0-0:Handle:unresolved  is_resolved=True conf=0.50\n  items[0].doWork()   dst=go:external:0-0:doWork:unresolved  is_resolved=True conf=0.85\n  r.Body.Close()      dst=go:external:0-0:Close:unresolved   is_resolved=True conf=0.85\n\nWHY THESE THREE SHAPES AND NOT THE FILED ONE. The filed repro\n(`tr := &http.Transport{}; tr.RoundTrip(req)`) is an IDENTIFIER receiver, and both\nguards that already stated the flag consume identifier receivers — so they shadow\nthese three for the obvious test input. Each sibling is reachable only via a\nnon-identifier receiver (index expression, field access). The first draft of the\nfixtures had all three collapse onto the already-correct WI-jopar guard and would\nhave passed while testing nothing; a non-vacuity floor now asserts the fixtures\nhit three DIFFERENT guards by their meta markers.\n\n*** BLAST RADIUS ON A SHIPPED MAP IS ZERO, AND I AM SAYING SO RATHER THAN\nSELLING IT. *** A/B on alertmanager, whole survey, both arms:\n    call edges            8,322  ->  8,322   (identical)\n    external call edges   1,576  ->  1,576   (identical)\n    external + is_resolved    0  ->      0   (identical)\n    confidence dist       {0.4: 1255, 0.5: 318, 0.8: 3} -> IDENTICAL\n    edges gained 0, lost 0\nfinalize's edge-resolution sub-step already flips the flag for an external dst,\nand since PR #248 it also re-derives confidence from its own verdict. So the\nproducer defect was being papered over downstream, exactly as this thread\npredicted. This is a latent-correctness fix for consumers that read edges BEFORE\nfinalize (tests, dst_ref derivation, anything holding analyzer output), and NO\nrecall or precision win is claimed from it. Same shape as INV-fokik.\n\nWHY THE ITEM STAYS VIOLATED. Its STATEMENT is about the live taint FP channel —\nan is_resolved=True external dst reaching the ungated hits[0] bare-name fallback.\nThe producer can no longer create that state, but the thread's own guidance is\nthat closing requires either (a) a non-tautological demonstration the channel is\nunreachable end-to-end, or (b) refiling the statement onto the mechanism that is\nreal. This note establishes the producer side only. The CONSUMER escape\n(`taint.py` ~485: `if not path_module: return hits[0]`) is untouched and still\nungated — any other producer, in any language, that sets the flag wrongly lands\non it. Option (b) plus a consumer-side decision is still the honest close.\n\nALSO STILL OPEN, unchanged: whether this shares a root cause with WI-kamin (Go\ninitializer typing hijacking 118/692 moved edges onto the wrong in-repo symbol).\nNot determined; not investigated here."  # 130d
- op: discuss  # 7286
  at: '2026-08-11T18:27:15Z'  # 7286
  by: agent  # 7286
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7286
  clock: 10  # 7286
  nonce: '7286'  # 7286
  message: "REORDERED BEHIND GO METHOD-KIND ATTRIBUTION, 2026-08-11, and here is the\nnon-tautological instrument this thread has asked for twice — designed, not run.\n\nWHY REORDERED. A prior session's handoff put this item first on the queue. That\nordering is STALE and I am recording why rather than silently dropping it. The\nproducer half is closed at every emit site (notes of 2026-08-10). What remains is\nthe CONSUMER escape, and this thread's own last note concedes \"the exploitability\nclaim through taint is NOT supported\". That makes the residual a coherence fix.\nThe standing owner directive ranks missing COVERAGE above refinement, so Go's\nmethod-kind catalogue gap (45 of 210 entries, 100% of the method-kind surface\nunattributed, measurement 0002) goes first. This item is not abandoned; it is\ncorrectly behind a recall item.\n\nTHE CONSUMER ESCAPE, RE-VERIFIED IN CODE ON dev 630598036b (not inherited):\n\n  taint.py:514-519, inside _match_propagation_entry (taint.py:414), is_resolved arm:\n      path_module = _module_from_symbol_path(edge_dst)\n      if not path_module:\n          return hits[0]          # <- UNGATED bare-name match; F3 never reached\n\n  _module_from_symbol_path (taint.py:1378) returns \"\" in exactly two cases:\n      (1) _extract_callee_module(edge_dst) is falsy, or\n      (2) it equals a member of _UNRESOLVED_MODULE_PLACEHOLDERS\n          (taint.py:328 = frozenset({\"external\", \"<external>\"})).\n\nWHY BOTH FILED MEASUREMENTS WERE TAUTOLOGIES, STATED STRUCTURALLY. finalize.py:397\n(_finalize_edge_resolution, ADR-0037 sub-step 7) sets is_resolved=True IF AND ONLY IF\nthe dst id is present in the final node set with kind != external_symbol. So\npost-finalize, entering the is_resolved arm at taint.py:491 asserts the dst is an\nin-repo node — and an in-repo node's path slot holds a real file path, which is\nneither empty nor a placeholder. The escape is therefore unreachable BY\nCONSTRUCTION for the ordinary case, which is why counting \"edges with\nis_resolved=True at an external path slot\" returns zero no matter when you sample.\nThat is a property of finalize's definition, not evidence about the branch.\n\nTHE TWO DOORS THAT SURVIVE THAT ARGUMENT — this is the part worth measuring:\n  (a) an in-repo node whose PATH SLOT is empty or is itself the literal placeholder.\n      Synthetic/linker-minted nodes are the candidate population (route nodes,\n      package nodes, manifest-derived symbols). Whether any exists with a\n      catalogue-colliding NAME is unknown.\n  (b) a MALFORMED dst id that _extract_callee_module cannot parse, which returns\n      falsy and lands on the same escape. INV-kurup and INV-dulah both record live\n      non-canonical id emission, so this population is not hypothetical.\nNeither door requires the producer bug this item was filed about. Both reach the\nsame ungated return.\n\nTHE INSTRUMENT (designed here so the next reader does not re-derive it):\nDO NOT re-implement the branch predicate — recomputing a production classification\nis itself the recurring bug in this project. OBSERVE THE LINE. Python here is\n3.12.3, so use sys.monitoring with set_local_events scoped to\n_match_propagation_entry's code object and a LINE handler, or coverage.py driven\nprogrammatically; either observes real execution of taint.py:519 with zero\nduplicate logic. Count executions of 519 AND of its siblings 527/528/532 — the\nsiblings are the NON-VACUITY FLOOR that proves the function ran and other arms\nfired, without which a zero at 519 is indistinguishable from \"the probe never\nattached\".\nPOSITIVE CONTROL IS MANDATORY AND CHEAP: call _match_propagation_entry directly\nwith is_resolved=True and a hand-made edge_dst whose module slot is \"external\" and\nwhose name collides with a catalogued entry. Line 519 must fire. Only after the\ncounter has been seen non-zero is a corpus zero worth anything.\n\nWHAT WOULD CLOSE THIS ITEM. Either (a) the instrument above reports zero across a\nmulti-language corpus WITH its positive control passing — which supports refiling\nthe statement onto the producer mechanism that was real and marking satisfied — or\n(b) it reports non-zero, in which case the escape is a live FP channel that no\nproducer fix can reach, and it should be refiled as a CONSUMER item and the doors\nabove are the population.\n\nUNCHANGED AND STILL OPEN: whether this shares a root cause with WI-kamin (Go\ninitializer typing hijacking 118/692 moved edges onto the wrong in-repo symbol).\nNot investigated here either."  # 7286
- op: discuss  # e36a
