  clock: 11  # e36a
  nonce: e36a  # e36a
  message: "THE NON-TAUTOLOGICAL MEASUREMENT THIS THREAD ASKED FOR, 2026-08-16, dev\n0d305fe0e4. Producer half CONFIRMED CLOSED on a real repo. Consumer half\nuntouched. Item stays violated on the consumer clause.\n\nI ALMOST FILED THE THIRD TAUTOLOGICAL MEASUREMENT. My first pass scanned shipped\nsurvey JSON -- alertmanager 16,904 edges and whisper.cpp 81,263 edges, 0\nviolations, positive control flagging a synthetic violating edge and negative\ncontrol clean. That evidence is WORTHLESS for this item and I am recording the\nnear-miss rather than the number: finalize's edge-resolution sub-step flips\nis_resolved for an external dst, so any post-finalize scan reports 0 whether or\nnot the producer is correct. The 2026-08-10 entry says exactly this and warns\nagainst a third such measurement. It was right.\n\nANALYZER-STAGE, WHICH IS WHERE THE DEFECT WOULD BE VISIBLE. analyze_go called\ndirectly on the repo, before finalize runs at all:\n\n    alertmanager, go call edges (analyzer stage)      15,532\n      ... with external/unresolved dst                 2,916\n      ... AND is_resolved=True (the filed shape)           0\n\n2,916 is a real denominator -- that is the population in which the defect could\nappear, and it is empty. Combined with the filed repro re-run at analyzer stage:\n\n    site_control   os.Create    module slot os        is_resolved=False\n    site_twostep   RoundTrip    module slot net/http  is_resolved=False\n    site_chained   RoundTrip    module slot external  is_resolved=False\n\nThe filed repro no longer reproduces, and not merely because the flag changed:\nsite_twostep now carries a REAL module slot (net/http) rather than the external\nplaceholder, so it matches through the module filter -- the legitimate path --\ninstead of the ungated hits[0] fallback. Go composite-literal receiver typing did\nthat; it is a different fix from the six go.py flag sites recorded on 2026-08-10,\nand it removes the input to the channel rather than the flag on it.\n\nSO THE STATEMENT AS WRITTEN NOW HOLDS FOR GO, with behavioural evidence at the\ncorrect pipeline stage and a meaningful denominator. That is the (a) half of the\nclose condition this thread set, for one language.\n\nWHY I AM NOT CLOSING IT. The (a) condition is \"the channel is unreachable\nEND-TO-END\", and the consumer escape is untouched -- taint.py:544, verified today:\n\n    path_module = _module_from_symbol_path(edge_dst)\n    if not path_module:\n        return hits[0]          # still ungated\n\nAny producer, in any language, that sets is_resolved=True on a dst with no path\nevidence still lands on an ungated bare-name match. Go can no longer create that\nstate; nothing prevents the next analyzer from doing so, and nothing would catch\nit if it did. Closing on the Go producer alone would be the partition-dressed-as-\nresolution shape this subsystem keeps being corrected for.\n\nRECOMMEND OPTION (b) FROM THE FILING, which this measurement now makes the\ncheaper path: refile the statement onto the CONSUMER -- \"a catalogue lookup must\nnot return a bare-name match for a dst whose path segment is the external\nplaceholder\" -- and let the Go producer clause close with the evidence above.\nThat converts a per-producer whack-a-mole into one chokepoint, which is what the\nfiling itself said (b) was.\n\nBEFORE SHIPPING THE CONSUMER GATE, and this is not a formality. It REMOVES\nmatches, and the same index backs SANITIZER registration -- losing a sanitizer\nmatch loses a barrier, and a lost barrier moves flows in the opposite direction\nfrom a lost sink. The filing already says measure both signs. Today's INV-nizom\nwork is a live warning about exactly this shape: a consumer rule that looked\nobviously correct removed 51 io-boundary matches on one repo, 49 of them TRUE\npositives, and was reverted after measurement. Measure on FINDINGS, both signs,\nbefore touching taint.py:544.\n\nSTILL NOT DETERMINED, unchanged: whether this shares a root cause with WI-kamin."  # e36a
