  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nCONSUMER CLAUSE RE-VERIFIED AT THE FILED LINE, STILL UNGATED. Read in code at dev 11a240f83d, taint.py:539-544:\n\n    path_module = _module_from_symbol_path(edge_dst)\n    if not path_module:\n        return hits[0]          # still ungated, line 544\n\nSo the 08-17 entry's finding holds unchanged: any producer, in any language, that sets is_resolved=True on a dst with no path evidence still lands on an ungated bare-name match.\n\nPRODUCER HALF, independently spot-checked rather than inherited: analyze_go on a fixture emits fh.Close() as go:external:0-0:Close:unresolved with call_construct=method and NO is_resolved key at all -- consistent with the 2,916-edge measurement finding zero of the filed shape.\n\nONE THING THAT DESERVES ITS OWN LINE, because it decides how urgent the consumer gate is: the consumers read the flag as edge.get('is_resolved', True) -- at taint.py:1790, 1853, 1965, 1981, 2893, 2908. The DEFAULT IS True. So an edge that carries no is_resolved key at all -- which is what every analyzer-stage go edge in my probe looked like -- is treated as RESOLVED. The producer fix removed the explicit True; it did not remove the True the consumer supplies on absence. That is worth confirming against the finalize stage before the consumer gate is designed.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: violated on the consumer clause. The thread's recommendation to refile the statement onto the consumer chokepoint is NOT applied here -- it changes what the item asserts, and the filing's own warning (measure on FINDINGS, both signs, before touching taint.py:544; INV-nizom removed 51 io-boundary matches, 49 of them TRUE) says that is a decision to take with a measurement in hand, not during a sweep."  # 3abd
